.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt IPC 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ipc
.Nd the one call of System V IPC
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft int
.Fn syscall SYS_ipc "unsigned int call" "int first" "unsigned long second" "unsigned long third" "void *ptr" "long fifth"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ipc ,
number 117, reaches every System V object through one call, as i386 Linux
has it, and musl makes it for all of them.
The low 16 bits of
.Fa call
name the operation, and the high 16 its version:
.Bl -tag -width "SEMTIMEDOP 4"
.It Dv SEMOP No 1
.Fn semop first ptr second .
.It Dv SEMGET No 2
.Fn semget first second third .
.It Dv SEMCTL No 3
.Fn semctl first second third ,
the fourth argument the word
.Fa ptr
points at.
.It Dv SEMTIMEDOP No 4
.Fn semtimedop first ptr second fifth ,
the timeout a 32-bit timespec.
.It Dv MSGSND No 11
.Fn msgsnd first ptr second third .
.It Dv MSGRCV No 12
.Fn msgrcv :
in version 0 the buffer and the type in a pair of words at
.Fa ptr ,
in version 1 the buffer at
.Fa ptr
and the type in
.Fa fifth ;
the size is
.Fa second
and the flags
.Fa third .
.It Dv MSGGET No 13
.Fn msgget first second .
.It Dv MSGCTL No 14
.Fn msgctl first second ptr .
.It Dv SHMAT No 21
.Fn shmat first ptr second ,
the address stored in the word at
.Fa third
and 0 returned; version 1 is
.Er EINVAL .
.It Dv SHMDT No 22
.Fn shmdt ptr .
.It Dv SHMGET No 23
.Fn shmget first second third .
.It Dv SHMCTL No 24
.Fn shmctl first second ptr .
.El
.Pp
x86-64 has no
.Nm ipc :
.Nm semget
(64),
.Nm semop
(65), which the kernel takes as
.Nm semtimedop
with no time limit,
.Nm semctl
(66),
.Nm semtimedop
(220),
.Nm msgget
(68),
.Nm msgsnd
(69),
.Nm msgrcv
(70),
.Nm msgctl
(71),
.Nm shmget
(29),
.Nm shmat
(30),
.Nm shmdt
(67) and
.Nm shmctl
(31) are calls of their own, and
.Dv IPC_STAT
fills the x86-64 records, whose times and sizes are 64-bit longs.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
What the operation returns.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
Another operation.
.El
.Pp
The operations fail as their pages say.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr msgget 2 ,
.Xr semget 2 ,
.Xr shmget 2
